From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:49:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: don't let the overscroll pan cancel page
 touches

OverscrollActionsController (pull to refresh, close tab, new tab) adds
a UIPanGestureRecognizer to the web view's scroll view. With WebKit that
is harmless: the scroll view scrolls with its own recognizer. With Blink
the page scrolls itself from the raw touches it receives, and the scroll
view only mirrors Blink's offset. Once the pan is recognized, a few
points into a drag, UIKit cancels those touches (cancelsTouchesInView
defaults to YES), so Blink gets touchcancel and stops scrolling.
RenderWidgetUIView removes the scroll view's recognizers when a new
render view attaches, which is why scrolling only failed some of the
time.

With Blink, keep the pan from cancelling or delaying touches.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator with a
page that logs touch events and scrollY: before, a 400 pt drag gave one
touchstart, then touchcancel and no scrolling; after, the page follows
the finger 1:1 (421 px for 416 px of travel) and a fast flick keeps
scrolling with momentum (955 px for 416 px). Pulling down at the top
still does nothing harmful.

diff --git a/ios/chrome/browser/overscroll_actions/ui_bundled/overscroll_actions_controller.mm b/ios/chrome/browser/overscroll_actions/ui_bundled/overscroll_actions_controller.mm
index e7fb4bd20b68e9f85bdae5a6f11aa87e4a5355f9..785d094c95e2fe2658afbf4e2d9af60623bb08be 100644
--- a/ios/chrome/browser/overscroll_actions/ui_bundled/overscroll_actions_controller.mm
+++ b/ios/chrome/browser/overscroll_actions/ui_bundled/overscroll_actions_controller.mm
@@ -698,6 +698,14 @@ - (void)setup {
   }
   [panGesture setMaximumNumberOfTouches:1];
   [panGesture setDelegate:self];
+#if BUILDFLAG(USE_BLINK)
+  // [ios-blink-sideload] With Blink the page scrolls itself from the raw
+  // touches it receives; the scroll view here only mirrors Blink's offset.
+  // Recognizing this pan must not cancel or delay those touches, or the page
+  // stops scrolling a few points into every drag.
+  panGesture.cancelsTouchesInView = NO;
+  panGesture.delaysTouchesEnded = NO;
+#endif
   [[self scrollView] addGestureRecognizer:panGesture];
   self.panGestureRecognizer = panGesture;
 }
